WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:36.070
Did Amuro's decision take effect?

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:39.140
Were Kamille's true strengths displayed?

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.400
Or were Four's strengths revealed...

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.950
...through her understanding of
Amuro and Kamille's desires?

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:46.920
In the midst of flames...

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:51.320
...Kamille overcame the force
of gravity and made it to space.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:57.120
A Sign of Zeta

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:02.900
And as Kamille returns to space...

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.900
...the Titans' fleet prepare for
Operation Apollo...

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:10.430
...a plan to conquer Von Braun City
on the near side of the Moon.

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:15.650
The Titans plan to display their power
through this operation...

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:20.780
...and gain control over the Earth
Federation Government and Spacenoids.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:41.900
Having a base on the far side
of the Moon...

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:44.770
...won't help intimidate the Earth
Federation Government.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:47.810
I see that the Spacenoids don't realize that.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.210
The Dogosse Gier has located us.

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:57.790
- The holoscope!
- Yes, sir!

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.490
He did well to find this ship.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:19.740
So, he's come.

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:24.540
He lives like a hermit,
yet as we see, he's quick to act.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:26.580
Yes, he's among the best.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:29.090
Paptimus Scirocco.
He could be dangerous.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:30.310
Unlikely, sir.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:33.920
His pledge of loyalty to you is sealed
with his blood, Your Excellency.

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:36.620
Scirocco's proposal.

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.490
Right, let me see it.

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:40.050
Yes, sir!

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.300
Yes, that's the one.

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:55.640
"I pledge my loyalty to you.
If ever I violate my pledge..."

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.650
"...you may take my life."

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.680
Paptimus Scirocco.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:08.260
A signature alone lacks credibility.

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:33.210
<i>Kamille.</i>

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:36.220
<i>At that rate, you'll get lost</i>
<i>even with minimal Minovsky particles.</i>

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.220
Roger! I'm coming in.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.190
<i>Make your report to the bridge in person.</i>

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.230
Roger.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:47.530
He just doesn't stop blabbing.
Heck, I'll make toast out of that Torres.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.400
- <i>I heard that.</i>
- Oops.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:08.120
It's been a full two days since
the Titans' fleet left Gryps, and yet...!

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:09.550
Captain.

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:13.020
Forward three.

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:15.120
We were unable to detect any
enemy movements.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:16.130
Thank you.

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:20.490
Which would mean the enemy's target
can't be Side Two.

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:22.290
I think it's the Moon.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:23.430
Granada?

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:27.630
But doesn't the fleet leaving
Gryps seem awfully small?

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:29.630
Kamille Bidan, reporting to bridge.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:32.330
Tell me about that
transport ship you encountered.

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:34.170
It belongs to the Colony Public
Corporation.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:37.440
It was no camouflage. They showed me
all the freight they're carrying.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:38.280
Good job.

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:39.580
Thank you, sir.

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:43.580
- Now, where could they...!
- Perhaps the near side of the Moon?

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:47.750
- What was that for?!
- You're being a pest!

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:50.520
I had to wake you up since you
were absentminded!

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.460
Cut it out!

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:53.330
Kamille, go and equip the Gundam!

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:54.490
Yes, sir.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.940
I understand your opinion,
Lieutenant Emma, but...!

00:05:59.000 --> 00:05:59.970
Kamille!

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:01.760
I'm not the least bit homesick!

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.900
Then why were you so out of it?!

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:06.840
Teach him a lesson!

00:06:06.910 --> 00:06:08.900
You think you've become
some sort of hero on Earth.

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:11.510
How dare you! Damn you!

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:12.480
Cut it out!

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:14.520
Those youngsters need to
let off some steam.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:16.450
This is the bridge!

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:20.650
You're all under confinement!

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.660
Remain in the disciplinary room
until I say it's okay!

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:24.200
Kamille started it!

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:25.490
You made fun of me!

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:27.330
I'm telling you to go to
the disciplinary room.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:28.370
Yes, sir.

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:34.270
- Come here a moment.
- Yes.

00:06:35.510 --> 00:06:36.740
I'll be waiting!

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:38.610
I'm not listening to any lectures.

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:42.080
You may have gained confidence
with your heroics on Earth...

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:43.670
...but it's different here in space.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.280
I don't believe I've grown
that arrogant.

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:49.080
You might not be homesick, but you're
suffering from something similar.

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:52.720
Being lonely is no reason to
take out your feelings on others.

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:55.220
Lonely? Me?

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:56.790
Boy, you're dim-witted.

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:58.830
No wonder you always snap at others.

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:00.060
I hope you're joking, for your sake.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.290
You don't even understand
your own feelings.

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:03.960
You shouldn't act like
you know everything.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.230
Come on.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:07.000
You fell in love while on Earth, right?

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:09.440
No way.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.610
I notified you that our ship
will be taking independent action.

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:23.250
<i>I only want to know why.</i>

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:27.410
Our unit is newly formed,
so we must assess our abilities.

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:30.660
We will join you in time
for Operation Apollo.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:31.320
<i>Very well.</i>

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:34.790
<i>But if you don't return in time</i>
<i>to commence the Operation...</i>

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:36.730
<i>...I won't hesitate</i>
<i>shooting you from behind.</i>

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:38.570
That's fine with me.

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:41.230
I'm happy to hear you say that, sir.

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:44.610
I'd like to see it used as an example
of a soldier's aspirations.

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:04.590
What incredible power. I could destroy
the Gundam Mk. II with a single shot!

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:05.790
<i>I'll test its transformation!</i>

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:06.990
Roger, Mouar!

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:11.830
Me too!

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:17.140
<i>This Gabthley is not bad at all!</i>

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:20.970
I have no idea what Scirocco's up to,
but I'll give it a try.

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:28.580
Scirocco?!

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.310
That's Scirocco's Messala.

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:36.220
In that case...!

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:38.360
Good move!

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.290
Lieutenant Scirocco.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:45.300
It is a pleasure to obtain
such a quality mobile suit.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:46.340
Thank you very much.

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:47.630
You've got good skills.

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:49.440
What I saw in you was no fluke.

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:58.380
I would be thrilled to have you
make use of those skills for me.

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:02.120
Damn Scirocco!

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:09.660
Excuse my rudeness for asking.

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:11.830
What is your objective,
Lieutenant Scirocco?

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:20.230
I believe my duties are to free people
whose souls are being pulled by gravity.

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:22.770
But those are the A.E.U.G.'s objectives.

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:24.070
Not true.

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:26.270
While the A.E.U.G.'s making all this fuss
in favor of space...

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:29.440
...they're no different than the people
of the Federation.

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:31.410
They're also bound to the Earth Sphere.

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:35.790
You seem to have an objection, Jerid.

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:38.950
Are you implying
that you're a Newtype?

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:42.820
I only sense that times will not change
unless I do something about it.

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:43.860
Nothing more.

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:48.960
Jamitov converted the Earth Federation
Forces to the Titans...

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:51.830
...to eradicate the people pulled by Earth.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:52.490
What?

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:57.910
By starting a war, he plans to exhaustively
force Earth's economy to the brink.

00:09:57.980 --> 00:10:00.210
People on Earth will die
of hunger and vanish.

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:04.910
On the surface, that sounds no different
from the A.E.U.G.'s objectives.

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:07.440
The point is after that.

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:14.890
The Earth Sphere's fate depends on
who rules humanity after the war.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:20.130
Don't you agree there'd be a need
for a genius to rule the Earth Sphere?

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:21.660
And you plan to be that person?

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:26.600
I believe the ruler of Earth after the war
will be a woman.

00:10:32.210 --> 00:10:33.270
Wake up!

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:36.380
You've got a nerve to sleep
in the disciplinary room!

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:39.040
Get up and stay up!

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:41.980
Stop giving him an excuse to yell.
You're wasting my rest time.

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:44.520
What else do you expect us to do?

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:47.820
Kamille, did you come across anything
interesting while on Earth?

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:50.720
Of course not!
I spent all my time escaping.

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:53.720
Any good holo-tapes from Hong Kong?

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:55.060
Yeah, yeah! Show us!

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:56.690
Not a chance!

00:10:56.770 --> 00:11:00.700
You know, I've always regarded you
as a great pilot.

00:11:00.770 --> 00:11:01.670
As a Newtype.

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:04.070
Now you're sounding sarcastic.

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:05.740
I apologize!

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:07.000
Yeah, we apologize!

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:11.320
Lieutenant Jerid's taken off.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:14.140
I sent him out to search for enemies.

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:17.340
I felt pressure from right fore.

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:21.820
I might have you go as well,
Ensign Mouar.

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:23.650
What do you mean by "pressure"?

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:25.700
It's difficult to explain verbally.

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:27.660
I'll be waiting on the mobile suit deck.

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:29.860
- Please do that.
- Yes, sir.

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:35.470
<i>Who's this low rank officer?</i>

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:37.300
<i>I haven't been introduced yet.</i>

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:46.010
It's easy for Scirocco
to say whatever he wants.

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:48.420
Well, say what you want.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:51.320
To me, you're just another enemy
I've got to step over!

00:11:56.390 --> 00:11:58.160
I can't believe my luck!

00:12:12.140 --> 00:12:14.040
<i>All units, take your battle positions!</i>

00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:16.810
What's this disciplinary room nonsense?!

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:19.410
They couldn't fight a war without us!

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:22.320
Stop bragging! What's so great about
rushing to your coffin?!

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:24.850
<i>There's one unit! Can't confirm affiliation!</i>
<i>Hurry with anti-air battery!</i>

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:25.890
<i>It's coming fast!</i>

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:28.190
Saegusa returning!

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:29.230
Good!

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:31.320
There's no way they'd attack
with one unit!

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:33.890
However, our optical camera
still only shows the one.

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:36.730
Coming in contact with the enemy
in this area...

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:40.730
...seems to indicate the Titans' fleet
is making a significant move.

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:41.460
Our mobile suits?!

00:12:41.540 --> 00:12:43.770
<i>Emma! Rick Dias! Ready for take off!</i>

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:45.240
<i>Any reinforcements?!</i>

00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:51.680
Emma unit, mounting catapult!

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:54.120
<i>Enemy appears to be only</i>
<i>the one mobile suit!</i>

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:55.740
<i>Search all surroundings!</i>

00:12:55.890 --> 00:12:56.880
I'm going!

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:07.760
Miss Emma, I'm not that immature.

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:10.060
- Enemies?!
- <i>Just the one, so far.</i>

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:12.500
That's impossible! Search for others!

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:14.370
Gundam Mk. II, taking off!

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:15.430
<i>Roger!</i>

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:23.810
That's strange! It's the same pattern
as back on Earth.

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:26.810
This feeling!

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:28.380
I must be about to face a new model!

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:34.630
Miss Emma.

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:37.320
Lieutenant Emma!

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:40.090
- What is it?
- This mobile suit is unusual.

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:41.700
<i>Be very cautious!</i>

00:13:41.770 --> 00:13:42.730
Roger.

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:46.560
Guys seem to suddenly come alive and
begin thinking clearly when going to war.

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:48.330
What's wrong with that?!

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:51.640
You're not my sister.

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:54.310
Watch out!

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:57.580
It's not a mobile suit?

00:13:57.650 --> 00:13:58.620
A battleship?

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:01.170
This mega particle cannon
has the force of a battleship's!

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:02.620
It's not a battleship, either.

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:05.090
A mobile armor?

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:06.380
It's possible.

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:12.300
That mobility proves it.

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:14.160
It's of a mobile suit class.

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:16.760
In addition, it holds the main cannon
of a battleship.

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:20.960
It didn't hit.

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:24.640
Looks like the aim still needs adjusting.

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:25.840
However...!

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:30.780
Kamille was right!
An unknown model is heading this way!

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:33.680
I was right! A new model!

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:41.760
It's no use! This guy's super
at close range battle as well!

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:44.590
It transformed!

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:50.830
It's coming!

00:14:52.140 --> 00:14:53.800
- Miss Emma! Move away!
- B-But...!

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:56.700
I can get it from this distance!

00:15:04.180 --> 00:15:05.510
Miss Emma!

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:11.020
Just because you're on a new model...!

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:12.920
What? This voice! Kamille!

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:17.930
He grazed me?! My rifle!

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:25.240
I wasn't aware that the Gundam Mk. II
had returned.

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:27.500
An enemy?

00:15:28.770 --> 00:15:30.740
Mouar!

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:37.250
I've come to assist you on Scirocco's orders.

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:39.280
- Are they coming?!
- Talk about unwanted help!

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:46.050
Kamille! You don't have time
to be helping me!

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:47.710
Get the enemy!

00:15:49.990 --> 00:15:52.390
Kamille! You can rescue me later!

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:55.420
It costs money to train pilots!

00:15:55.500 --> 00:15:59.330
Nemo, number 24! Take the Rick Dias
escape pod back to the Argama!

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:04.580
Above?!

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:11.940
You showing your back to me?!

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:17.350
There are two units!

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:23.760
Jerid! What are you hesitating for?!
Use the cannon!

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:26.800
This one's not like the other machines!

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.190
I'm going to torture it to death.

00:16:34.110 --> 00:16:36.130
Kamille! Die!

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:37.700
What?!

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:42.470
My hatch opened!

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:48.750
Mouar! A new enemy!

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:54.820
It came from a completely
different direction!

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:57.260
It can't be the Argama!

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:06.370
That was careless of me!
I didn't expect two new models.

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:08.230
Is this the immaturity they're referring to?

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:10.660
<i>Gundam Mk. II, respond!</i>

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:13.840
I was useless in the battlefield.
How could I...?

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:16.640
Am I to suffocate out here...

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:22.010
...and join my parents?

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:24.820
<i>Mk. II, respond!</i>

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:26.190
Fa.

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:30.190
Where is it?!

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:39.900
I see it! It's a small transport ship!

00:17:50.310 --> 00:17:51.370
Jerid, retreat!

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:54.150
It's using a powerful mega particle cannon!

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:09.360
Where's that fighter from?

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:11.570
Is it one of the A.E.U.G.'s new models?!

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:40.930
Fa!

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.000
Are you okay, Kamille?

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:46.100
I-I want to retrieve the Gundam Mk. II...

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:48.870
...and the enemy's still out there!
They're new models!

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:51.470
Lieutenant Apolly's brought Zeta here.

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:52.270
Zeta?!

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:54.070
- Zeta Gundam!
- Zeta's been completed?!

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:02.880
I've never seen that model before!

00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:05.050
Fall!

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:07.880
Once more!

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:15.130
Jerid!

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:16.560
Are you all right?! Are you alive?!

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:22.070
I'm not about to die
with something like this!

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:23.540
<i>We're escaping! Come over here!</i>

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:24.580
Okay!

00:19:35.290 --> 00:19:36.550
Did I get it?

00:19:40.060 --> 00:19:43.930
But there should be one more.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:45.460
It's from the Argama!

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:49.660
I wonder if Lieutenant Apolly saw that.

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:52.570
But we could destroy the enemy
if we pursued it in the Zeta.

00:19:52.640 --> 00:19:53.600
You're wrong.

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:59.410
A pilot doesn't see everything
that happens on the battlefield.

00:20:00.110 --> 00:20:03.140
He can't see what's going on
in other parts of space.

00:20:03.210 --> 00:20:04.510
That's why orders are a must.

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:06.640
I'm impressed, Kamille.

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:09.720
Never mind, Kamille.

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:15.390
We need to retrieve the Gundam Mk. II.

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:16.360
Okay!

00:20:16.430 --> 00:20:18.260
Argama, can you hear me?

00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:19.230
<i>Loud and clear!</i>

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:20.860
Has Lieutenant Emma been rescued?!

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:23.960
<i>Done! Hurry with the retrieval</i>
<i>of the Gundam!</i>

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:25.540
Roger!

00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:38.550
No fractures.

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:39.910
Nothing serious.

00:20:39.980 --> 00:20:41.510
Just bruises and I'm out.

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:42.350
How clumsy of me.

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:44.650
To the contrary. Your daily training's
made you tougher.

00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:49.450
How's Lieutenant Jerid?

00:20:49.530 --> 00:20:52.050
- Just some bruises, it seems.
- That's good to hear.

00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:54.220
However...!

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:57.030
What are you trying to say?

00:20:57.700 --> 00:21:00.500
An adult is better off with a grown man.

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:03.560
If you have a particular fetish for boys,
that's fine...

00:21:03.910 --> 00:21:06.970
...but I'm the only one with the ability
to fulfill your ambitions.

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:13.280
As long as you remain ambitious,
you'd be wise not to forget that.

00:21:16.020 --> 00:21:16.990
What is it with this guy?

00:21:21.830 --> 00:21:23.820
Here's a chart on the fleet's progress.

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:27.060
What about Lieutenant Quattro's message?

00:21:27.130 --> 00:21:28.860
That's fine, Fa Yuiry.

00:21:29.270 --> 00:21:30.500
Thank you, sir.

00:21:30.570 --> 00:21:33.560
I'll be excused.

00:21:33.940 --> 00:21:34.770
Lieutenant Apolly!

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:36.110
Hi!

00:21:36.170 --> 00:21:39.140
I didn't see the Zeta's manual in the cockpit.

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:41.470
It's in here. I'll brief you on it later.

00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:43.880
- Please.
- Sure.

00:21:50.150 --> 00:21:53.020
- Long time no see.
- Yeah!

00:21:55.590 --> 00:21:57.530
Fa, I wanted so badly to see you!

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:04.960
Please let me hold you for now.

00:22:18.280 --> 00:22:19.610
Are you becoming a pilot?

00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:21.310
That's my intention.

00:22:22.090 --> 00:22:24.490
- You couldn't do it.
- Can you be so sure?

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.390 --> 00:23:47.750
Kamille is being unfriendly to Fa.

00:23:48.520 --> 00:23:51.050
Conscious of the presence
of Scirocco and Yazan...

00:23:51.130 --> 00:23:53.090
...Jerid throws himself into the battle scene.

00:23:53.190 --> 00:23:57.100
However, he struggles against
the Argama's new forces.

00:23:58.270 --> 00:24:02.460
As Paptimus observes this,
what could be going through his mind?

00:24:03.470 --> 00:24:07.540
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"The Eyes of Scirocco".

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
The Eyes of Scirocco

00:24:09.310 --> 00:24:12.470
You will see the tears of time.
